BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm (The allocation bitmap records available blocks. Directories use hash-table slots and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (chains of file or directory header blocks, with Amiga metadata including names,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (protections, timestamps and file comments. File extension blocks expand the pointer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (capacity when a file exceeds what its header can describe. The storage layout must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 608.0 Tm (interpreted with the correct block size and partition origin.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (FFS reuses much of the Amiga namespace model but can differ between international,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (directory-cache and long-name types. Case folding, caching state and name limits are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (mode-dependent. Hard-link and symbolic-link representations are not automatically) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 527.0 Tm (identical to the full semantics of a Unix VFS.) Tj ET
