BT /F2 14 Tf 0.02 0.45 0.50 rg 1 0 0 1 50 711.0 Tm (INTEGRITY AND RECOVERY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm (FFS does not have a general journal comparable to ext3 or NTFS. The root block can contain) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (a bitmap-valid flag, and metadata must be checked before write access after an interrupted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (operation. File data no longer has the OFS header and checksum redundancy, so recovery) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (relies more heavily on trustworthy file header and extension-block references.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 595.0 Tm (A checker should validate directory hash chains, file headers, bitmap use, checksum) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (fields, block ownership and reference completeness. Reconstruction from raw data is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (inherently more speculative than on OFS because ownership sequence numbers are not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (available in each data block. The ability to recover a partly overwritten file must not be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 527.0 Tm (exaggerated.) Tj ET
