BT /F1 8 Tf 0.34 0.40 0.44 rg 1 0 0 1 512 34.0 Tm (PAGE 06) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 0.02 0.45 0.50 rg 1 0 0 1 50 711.0 Tm (DESIGN RATIONALE AND LIMITATIONS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm (FFS trades some of OFS's per-block redundancy for greater throughput and data capacity per) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (block, an appropriate choice for hard disks. The format remains bitmap-and-header based) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (rather than a FAT or B-tree filesystem. Its layout must account for reserved blocks and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (the root block's geometry.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 595.0 Tm (A modern implementation should support multiple legitimate block sizes, DOS types and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (Amiga partitioning conventions, including RDB. Neither an Amiga filesystem name nor a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (partition size is sufficient to identify data-block semantics. The FFS improvements did) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (not add end-to-end checksums or a full modern transaction model.) Tj ET
