BT /F2 13.5 Tf 0.02 0.44 0.50 rg 1 0 0 1 50 710 Tm (DISK READ PATH / ENGINEERING NOTES) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 678 Tm (1. Verify the boot-block DOS identifier and the appropriate FFS variant before processing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 661.5 Tm (block headers, filenames and directory metadata.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 635 Tm (2. Unlike OFS, FFS file data blocks are raw payload data without the 24-byte OFS header.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 618.5 Tm (The difference affects throughput and the amount of usable data per block.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 592 Tm (3. Root and directory header blocks still contain hash tables and links for namespace) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 575.5 Tm (lookup; FFS did not replace the directory system with a FAT.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 549 Tm (4. Follow directory hash chains with checksums and type validation. File and extension) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 532.5 Tm (header blocks carry the file's table of data-block references.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 506 Tm (5. Interpret Amiga big-endian metadata, file timestamps, protection bits, comments and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 489.5 Tm (name lengths using the selected DOS variant's rules.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 463 Tm (6. Block pointers are partition-relative. The root placement and bitmap positions cannot) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 446.5 Tm (be inferred safely from a generic partition table without checking volume geometry.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 420 Tm (7. Treat international and directory-cache format variants as real on-media differences,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 403.5 Tm (not merely mount-time performance switches.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 377 Tm (8. Check logical file length independently of the number of referenced blocks, especially) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 360.5 Tm (for partially filled final blocks and recovered file headers.) Tj ET
